---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { getUrl } from '../../utils/nav';
---

<BaseLayout title="Go-To-Market & Deal-Making Process Overhaul" description="Project detail">
  <main class="page-shell project-detail-shell">
    <article class="project-detail">
      <div class="project-header">
        <a href={getUrl('/projects')} class="back-link"><span aria-hidden="true">←</span> All case studies</a>
        <h1>Go-To-Market & Deal-Making Process Overhaul</h1>
        <p class="project-intro">Rebuilt the way a sales and customer-facing team translated product value into a consistent, repeatable deal process.</p>
      </div>

      <div class="project-meta-grid">
        <div class="meta-item">
          <span class="meta-label">Client:</span>
          <span class="meta-value">Sales & customer operations</span>
        </div>
        <div class="meta-item">
          <span class="meta-label">Role:</span>
          <span class="meta-value">UX researcher & strategy partner</span>
        </div>
        <div class="meta-item">
          <span class="meta-label">Focus:</span>
          <span class="meta-value">Workflow mapping, sales enablement, operational design</span>
        </div>
        <div class="meta-item">
          <span class="meta-label">Preview:</span>
          <a href="#" class="meta-link">View project →</a>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="project-content">
        <section class="content-section">
          <h2>Creating a coherent path from customer need to commercial decision</h2>
          <p>The sales team's approach to deal-making was inconsistent, with high variability in how they positioned value and moved deals forward. We needed to understand the root causes and design a repeatable process that would reduce complexity and clarify team handoffs.</p>
          <p>Through workflow mapping and stakeholder interviews, we identified key pain points and designed a coherent customer journey that the team could follow consistently. This work reduced variability and helped the team communicate more effectively.</p>
        </section>
      </div>
    </article>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
